# The interview clips are Git LFS objects — 142 MB of video that must never
# enter Git history as blobs. These two lines were dropped when the eol rules
# below were added, and the very next `git add -A` smudged all five pointers
# into their real binaries and staged 148 MB for the push.
*.MP4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Server-side scripts and configs are consumed by Linux. core.autocrlf=true is
# set on the dev machine, so without this they come back CRLF on checkout and
# the shebang line becomes `/usr/bin/env bash\r` — "no such file or directory".
*.sh            text eol=lf
deploy/*.conf   text eol=lf
deploy/*.service text eol=lf
